  "description": "T1; Robinia - Remove deadwood and reduce the two lowest limbs growing over the garden from 5 m to 3 m each.\rT2: Birch - Reduce the height by 1.5m, returning to the previous pruning points, and reduce the sides to match. Remove deadwood, crossing branches and trunk suckers.\rT3: Robinia - 2m Crown reduction to previous pruning points, remove deadwood, crossing branches and trunk suckers.\rT4: Poplar: Reduce the crown to the previous pruning points at the level of the observed hollow, reducing the height by 8m, remove deadwood.\rT5: Oak - Selectively lift the crown by removing approximately three lower limbs. Overall height remains the same.\rT6: Ash - Reduce the crown to the previous pruning points, reducing the height by 2.5m, remove deadwood, crossing branches and trunk suckers.\rT7: Ash - Reduce the crown to the previous pruning points, reducing the height by 2m. Remove deadwood, crossing branches and trunk suckers.\rT8: Oak - Reduce the crown to the previous pruning points, reducing the height by 2m. Remove deadwood, crossing branches and trunk suckers.",
